QQVibe
Based on tswawa/WechatVibe 1.2.2 (Apache-2.0).
Upstream source: https://github.com/tswawa/WechatVibe
Baseline: 02b770821a1cf46b8ecc46b4f874ac6f922bd586
QQVibe adds/adapts QQ account and message storage, QCE read-only connectors,
import, synchronization, analysis scopes, desktop identity and UI.
Original copyright and license notices remain in source files and
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Embedded Laya source attribution is preserved in
electron/laya/NOTICE and electron/laya/LICENSE.
QQVibe is independently maintained and is not affiliated with Tencent,
WechatVibe upstream, Convai Innovations, or the model port authors.

The full portable package redistributes fixed Laya ONNX model files under
Apache-2.0. Original model: Convai Innovations and Laya contributors.
Original revision: 052592a15d198d9ad47da779604259b10b47b7aa
MLX conversion: aac6fef/laya-multilingual-mlx, f2b4faf51023039425946074e2cf1361d2db11d5
ONNX conversion: mizchi/laya-multilingual-onnx, d9d003d543e63d6d3375c21d44624136bd1e0bad
QQVibe does not retrain these weights. Conversion descriptions, original model
card and applicable upstream LICENSE/NOTICE are retained in licenses/ and
resources/client/.models/laya/README.md in the full package.
